# Third-party notices for rekt-oss-mma

The `rekt-oss-mma` image contains locally patched open-source components.

| Component | Source | License |
|---|---|---|
| cobol-rekt / smojol `v0.1.0-RC6` | https://github.com/avishek-sen-gupta/cobol-rekt | MIT; see `LICENSE.cobol-rekt` |
| Local patches and image packaging | This repository | MIT; see `LICENSE` |
| che-che4z-lsp-for-cobol dialect adapters | https://github.com/eclipse/che-che4z-lsp-for-cobol | EPL-2.0 |
| Eclipse Temurin 21 | https://adoptium.net/ | GPLv2 with Classpath Exception |
| Graphviz | https://graphviz.org/ | EPL-2.0 |
| SnakeYAML 2.5 | https://bitbucket.org/snakeyaml/snakeyaml | Apache-2.0 |

The host preprocessing support also bundles Broadcom's unmodified SQLDA parser
copybook under EPL-2.0. Its source revision, hash and license attribution are
documented in `docs/bundled-system-copybooks.md`; its original notice is retained.

The image builds cobol-rekt from source and applies the patches under
`patches/`. The upstream source remains owned and licensed by its respective
copyright holders.

Local changes also include explicit target-analysis profiles, documented platform
service binding, and native COMP-1/COMP-2 layout metadata. The accompanying profile
links to IBM documentation; it does not include IBM runtime implementation code.
Further local changes preserve DB2 null-indicator boundaries and bind supported
CICS task operands, local labels and source-backed local LINK dependencies.
Further extensions bind explicit shared SQL declarations and supported BMS-derived
symbolic layouts to their actual inputs, and retain channel/async CICS commands
with catalog-backed finite transaction routing and symbolic completion values.
Additional local changes bind supported INQUIRE ASSOCIATION origin-data operands
and explicit, documented BMS attribute replacement contracts to original source
and derived screen layouts. These contracts contain no IBM SDK copybook bytes.
